# Implementation Plan - Phase 2 Improvements

This plan details the implementation of four core improvements: mobile number validation, blood units validation, persistent user statistics, and functional donor availability matching.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - Statistics increment is securely tied to the existing successful `completeBloodDonation` endpoint to ensure they cannot be double-counted.
> - The database changes are backward-compatible and handle legacy users by defaulting missing values to `0` or `false`.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend Components

---

#### [MODIFY] [User.js](file:///c:/Users/croma/OneDrive/Desktop/BloodBridge/server/models/User.js)
- Add new fields:
  - `donationsCount: { type: Number, default: 0 }`
  - `bloodReceivedCount: { type: Number, default: 0 }`
- Ensure `availableToDonate: { type: Boolean, default: false }` is properly declared.

#### [MODIFY] [authController.js](file:///c:/Users/croma/OneDrive/Desktop/BloodBridge/server/controllers/authController.js)
- Update responses for `registerUser`, `loginUser`, and `updateLocation` to serialize the new stats: `donationsCount`, `bloodReceivedCount`.
- Update `getUserProfile` (GET `/profile`) to:
  - Retrieve the user profile from the database.
  - Dynamically query `BloodRequest.countDocuments({ requestedBy: userId })` to get the count of requests created by this user.
  - Add `requestsCreatedCount` to the user profile response object.

#### [MODIFY] [bloodRequestController.js](file:///c:/Users/croma/OneDrive/Desktop/BloodBridge/server/controllers/bloodRequestController.js)
- In `createBloodRequest`:
  - Validate `contactNumber` matches `/^\d{10}$/` (exactly 10 digits, no characters). Return `400` status on failure.
  - Validate `unitsRequired` is an integer between 1 and 6. Return `400` status on failure.
- In `getBloodRequests`:
  - Enforce donor visibility: if the current user has `availableToDonate !== true`, return an empty list `[]` for `availableRequests`.

#### [MODIFY] [donorResponseController.js](file:///c:/Users/croma/OneDrive/Desktop/BloodBridge/server/controllers/donorResponseController.js)
- In `submitDonorResponse`:
  - Verify `donor.availableToDonate === true`. If false, return a `400` error: `"You must be available to donate to respond to requests"`.
- In `completeBloodDonation` (the final step in the donation workflow):
  - After validating the donation completion to prevent double-counting, increment `donationsCount` for the donor (`response.donor`) and increment `bloodReceivedCount` for the request owner (`bloodRequest.requestedBy`).

